  "body": "This PR needs the maintainer's decision. It changes a workflow in `.github/`. The runner tokens for more `camcraft-post-merge` runners come separately; this PR adds no secret and no repository variable.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `.github/workflows/post-merge.yml`: the concurrency group is per commit, `post-merge-${{ inputs.ref || github.sha }}`, with `cancel-in-progress: false`. Each push runs on a free `camcraft-post-merge` runner and always finishes. The `gate` job does not change.\n- The `report` job has its own concurrency group, `post-merge-report`, with `cancel-in-progress: false`. Its checkout uses `fetch-depth: 0`.\n- `.github/scripts/post-merge-report.sh` keeps the last reported commit in a hidden marker in the rolling issue body: `<!-- post-merge-last-sha: <sha> -->`.\n  - The script reads the marker from the newest rolling issue, open or closed.\n  - If this commit is an ancestor of the marker commit and is not the same commit, the script prints a notice and reports nothing (`git merge-base --is-ancestor`).\n  - Otherwise it reports as before and writes the marker. A new red issue carries the marker in its body. A green run with no open issue writes the marker into the last closed issue.\n  - If git cannot resolve a sha, the script reports as before.\n- The red issue text now says that each run gates exactly one commit.\n- `docs/decisions/3184-post-merge-per-commit.md` records the decision.\n\n## Cause\n\nOne concurrency group for `main` let one run go at a time. A second push waited, and a third push cancelled the waiting run. A red run then covered several merges, and the breaking merge needed a bisect (#3111).\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (all in xtask):\n- `post_merge_concurrency::post_merge_runs_each_commit_on_its_own`: the group is per commit and `cancel-in-progress` is false.\n- `post_merge_concurrency::post_merge_reports_one_at_a_time_with_full_history`: the report job has group `post-merge-report`, `cancel-in-progress: false` and `fetch-depth: 0`.\n- `post_merge_report::order::*` (6 tests, unix only): the real script runs against a temporary git repository with two commits and a fake `gh` that records each call.\n  - `an_older_green_run_never_closes_a_newer_red_issue`\n  - `an_older_red_run_never_reopens_after_a_newer_green_run`\n  - `a_newer_green_run_closes_the_issue_and_moves_the_marker`\n  - `a_green_run_without_an_open_issue_records_its_commit`\n  - `a_new_red_issue_carries_the_marker`\n  - `the_same_commit_reports_again`\n\nMutation results:\n- The upstream script with the new tests: 5 order tests red. The new script: 7 of 7 green.\n- The upstream workflow: 2 of 2 concurrency tests red. The new workflow: 2 of 2 green.\n- The guard without the \"not the same commit\" check: `the_same_commit_reports_again` red. Restored: green.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (xtask unit tests). `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real Actions run. The workflow change runs only after a merge to `main`.\n- The real `gh` with `--jq`. The fake `gh` returns the final values directly.\n- GitHub keeps at most one pending job in a concurrency group. If three report jobs wait at once, GitHub cancels the middle one, and that report is lost until the next run on `main`. The decision file records this limit.\n- The `runners` skill (`.claude/skills/runners/SKILL.md`) still says \"A group of merges tests only the newest head\". The edit of that file was refused in this session (a protected path). A follow-up must change that line.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes these files.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3184\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
